// integration-tests/coherent-sets -- wire types.
//
// A vehicle telemetry publisher must never let a subscriber observe a
// Position update without its paired Velocity update (or vice versa) -- the
// real-world reason GROUP coherent sets exist. Position and Velocity are
// deliberately two separate topics (not two instances of one topic) so this
// scenario exercises GROUP-scope coherence across *writers*, not just
// per-instance history within one writer. See
// docs/design/integration-test-tier.md for the full scenario spec.
// Byte-identical copy required in c/, cpp/, java/, zig/ (same discipline
// every other integration-tests/examples app follows).
@final
struct Position {
    int32 group_id;
    double x;
    double y;
};

@final
struct Velocity {
    int32 group_id;
    double vx;
    double vy;
};
